# Structs named by this server. Upstream `struct.sym` is empty, so nothing here can collide.
#
# Every entry is a **vanilla** struct: the Leagues relic definitions ship in the rev 233 cache
# without symbol names, and `find()` can only reach a named type. These alias the real ids on
# purpose - they mint nothing. The set is the one `league_relics` draws for `league_type` 5, read
# from `enum 5702` (tiers) and each tier's param-878 enum (relics, 1-based). `RelicTableTest`
# re-walks that chain against `Relic` so a cache upgrade that moves a relic fails loudly.
1117	league_relic_power_miner
1119	league_relic_lumberjack
1118	league_relic_animal_wrangler
1123	league_relic_corner_cutter
1124	league_relic_friendly_forager
1125	league_relic_dodgy_deals
1120	league_relic_clue_compass
1121	league_relic_bank_heist
1725	league_relic_fairys_flight
1131	league_relic_golden_god
1127	league_relic_reloaded
1736	league_relic_equilibrium
1128	league_relic_treasure_arbiter
1723	league_relic_production_master
1129	league_relic_slayer_master
1130	league_relic_total_recall
4719	league_relic_bankers_note
1126	league_relic_pocket_kingdom
1132	league_relic_grimoire
1133	league_relic_overgrown
1134	league_relic_specialist
4728	league_relic_guardian
1135	league_relic_last_stand
# The league itself and its eight relic tiers, also vanilla. `enum 2670[5]` is the Raging Echoes
# struct; its param 870 enum lists the tier structs in order. Named so editors can point the
# league's task list (param 868) at ours and lower each tier's points threshold (param 877).
6211	league_raging_echoes
1136	league_tier_1
1137	league_tier_2
1138	league_tier_3
1139	league_tier_4
1140	league_tier_5
1141	league_tier_6
1142	league_tier_7
1143	league_tier_8
# League tasks, authored by this server and packed at `50000 + id` ("ours start at 50000",
# as in `.local/param.sym`). The id is the task's position in `LeagueTasks` and is frozen for
# life: it is also the completion bit the client reads and the key the counters are saved under.
# `LeagueTaskTableTest` regenerates this block from the table and fails if it differs, so edit
# the Kotlin table and paste the block it prints rather than editing these lines by hand.
